Then quantH2O loops kk=1:length(metsName.metab{mm,ss}) — metsName.metab{1,1} = 'Cr' — length of 'Cr' = 2!! That's a char array of length 2. Hmm, then `lookUpRelaxTimes(metsName.metab{mm,ss},Bo)` — passes 'Cr' whole, and indexes T1_Metab(kk) for kk=1,2. lookUpRelaxTimes('Cr','7T') returns the Cr relax times presumably.

So both rows of ampl (metab_signal; metab_signal) get the same correction. Fine.

